meta {
  name: Import PHI Rules
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/phi-config/import
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "csv": "pattern,maskingType,alwaysMasked,database,table\n*ssn*,FULL,true,,\n*email*,PARTIAL,false,,"
  }
}

docs {
  Import PHI masking rules from CSV content (`csv` = raw file text). Header row is required with at least `pattern` and `maskingType` columns; column order is free, `maskingType` is FULL | PARTIAL | HASH | REDACT, `alwaysMasked` accepts true/false/1/0/yes/no (default false), max 1000 data rows. Any validation error rejects the whole file (400 with per-line `errors`). Rows are matched to existing rules on pattern + database + table (case-insensitive): identical rows are skipped (never duplicated), rows with a different maskingType/alwaysMasked update the existing rule, new rows are inserted — all in one transaction. Returns `{ imported, updated, skipped, total }` and writes a PHI_RULES_IMPORT audit entry.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
  **Admin only.**
}
